Context:
- Added Scheme development environment configuration for SquiggleConf 2025 project
- Integrated tmux session management with project-specific Emacs configurations
- Supports Guile 3 with full Geiser integration for REPL-driven development

Considerations:
- Uses direnv-compatible .envrc for environment setup
- Provides both general conference note-taking and specialized Scheme development configs
- Tmux sessions are named after project for easy identification
- Emacs launched with -Q flag for clean environment, loading only project configs

Technical Details:
- squiggleconf-scheme.el provides complete Scheme IDE features
- Paredit for structural editing of S-expressions
- TRAMP support for remote development
- Org-mode integration for literate programming with Scheme
- Company mode for intelligent code completion
- Rainbow delimiters for visual parenthesis matching

Issues Addressed:
- Provides isolated development environment per project
- Enables consistent Scheme tooling across different machines
- Supports both local and remote REPL connections

Timing:
- Implementation completed: 2025-08-06
- Tested with Guile 3.x on FreeBSD 14.3

Usage:
- Run "make tmux-scheme" to start Scheme development environment
- Run "make tmux-emacs" for general conference note-taking environment
- Source .envrc to get start_project_emacs function in shell
